Week 3 Documentation
In Week 3, we improved our microcontroller simulator by adding Memory, Stack, and FIFO Queue functions.
The main aim was to make the simulator more functional and to understand how these components work with the CPU.

Objectives
Add Read and Write operations for Memory.
Connect Memory with the simulator.
Add Stack Pointer (SP).
Add PUSH and POP operations.
Display the Stack and SP.
Add FIFO Queue.
Add Enqueue and Dequeue operations.
Check whether the Queue follows FIFO order.
Prepare a Queue flowchart.
Create an Assembly program to test the Queue.
Test Memory, Stack, and Queue.
Update the project documentation.
